:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CHGDIRSVRA.Change Directory Server Attr (CHGDIRSVRA)
:P.Use the Change Directory Server Attributes (CHGDIRSVRA) command to
set the administrator of a directory server instance and its password,
or the password of the instance's update distinguished name. The values
go to the instance's configuration file; a new password is used at once.
You need *ALLOBJ and *IOSYSCFG special authorities.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDIRSVRA/INSTANCE'.Instance (INSTANCE)
:P.The directory server instance to change, as the instance list names
it. QUSRDIR is the instance every system has.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QUSRDIR is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDIRSVRA/DN'.Distinguished name (DN)
:P.The distinguished name to change and its new password. The password
is kept as a salted hash, never as typed.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.Nothing is changed.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Distinguished name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ADMINDN:EPK.
:PD.The administrator's password changes; the administrator stays the
one the instance has (cn=Administrator unless changed).
:PT.:PK.*UPDATEDN:EPK.
:PD.The password of the update distinguished name changes. Replication
is not supported, so nothing binds with it.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Password
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
